[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human HCC tumor (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=9,160): skew = -0.505, excess kurtosis = 0.179, D'Agostino K^2 p = 7.99e-79, Jarque-Bera p = 4.53e-88
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.502, excess kurtosis = 0.560, D'Agostino K^2 p = 5.24e-92, Jarque-Bera p = 2.42e-110
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 278.135, p = 1.77e-29
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 28.618, p = 4.08e-13
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/ribonn/HCC_tumor/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_te_histogram_ribonn_HCC_tumor.png
